From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The pause menu no longer quits a game started from the command line

The SDL frontend handles a paused VM and a shut down one in the same branch
of its CPU thread loop: with nothing pending and no FullscreenUI session
(a game passed on the command line, which is how EmulationStation starts
every one), it takes the game for finished and quits. Opening the pause
menu (Select+X here) paused the VM, the menu showed for half a second and
PCSX2 closed as if the game had ended. Only a VM that is gone ends the
frontend now; a paused one gets the input pumping the FullscreenUI idle
state has, so its menu works (Resume, Close Game and the rest).

diff --git a/pcsx2-sdl/Main.cpp b/pcsx2-sdl/Main.cpp
index aabd81690..12d830f0a 100644
--- a/pcsx2-sdl/Main.cpp
+++ b/pcsx2-sdl/Main.cpp
@@ -813,10 +813,12 @@ void Pcsx2SDL::CPUThreadMain(VMBootParameters initial_params, bool start_in_fsui
 					continue;
 				}
 
-				// Nothing pending. If no FSUI session is running, exit cleanly
-				// — the user's game finished and there is no UI to show next,
-				// so the frontend's job is done.
-				if (!start_in_fsui)
+				// Nothing pending. If the VM is gone and no FSUI session is
+				// running, exit cleanly — the user's game finished and there
+				// is no UI to show next, so the frontend's job is done. A
+				// paused VM is not finished: its pause menu is up, and it
+				// needs the same input pumping as the FSUI idle state below.
+				if (state == VMState::Shutdown && !start_in_fsui)
 				{
 					s_shutdown_requested.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
 					break;
